ace":"சிறுவழி","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறு","gloss":"small"},{"text":"வழி","lemma":"வழி","gloss":"path"}],"gloss":"narrow path"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"படஞ்செய்","parts":[{"text":"படம்","lemma":"படம்","gloss":"cloth/canopy"},{"text":"செய்","lemma":"செய்","gloss":"made"}],"gloss":"made of cloth"},{"surface":"பந்தர்க்","parts":[{"text":"பந்தர்க்","lemma":"பந்தர்க்","gloss":"canopy"}],"gloss":"canopy","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கல்மிசை","parts":[{"text":"கல்","lemma":"கல்","gloss":"stone"},{"text":"மிசை","lemma":"மிசை","gloss":"upon"}],"gloss":"upon the stone"},{"surface":"யதுவே","parts":[{"text":"யதுவே","lemma":"யதுவே","gloss":"is indeed"}],"gloss":"is indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"To grow even if touched, snatching and twisting / sad tune bringing sweet playing, not thinking of / fainting heart attaining, the wife / stroking hair looking at, of the saline wasteland / cactus shade deity having praised / hungry waist melting with sorrow, worshiping with hands / 'I do not see, is it so?' saying, you who ask, who comes / O bard, listen! Of prosperity, the state indeed / gift receiving you will eat, even if, begging having set out / grief you will have, even if, both / are in hand, it seems, quickly very near / front village battle because of, having appeared, his own village / large herd of cattle gathered, brave warriors / discharged arrows flood, drum-raft as / victory having given, killing and seizing having rescued / the world to lament, encircled snake's / sharp teeth escaped moon like, warriors / from the hands escaped possessing calves many cows / with the herd who came, man of fame having become / shed skin snake resembling, himself indeed / difficult to reach world to, he went, the body indeed / forest small river steep bank having fixed its base / with the post shaken target like / with arrows to shake, there perished indeed / high fame abundantly appeared name indeed / gentle peacock beautiful feathers having adorned / space for others not taking narrow path / made of cloth canopy upon the stone is indeed","translation":"O bard, who comes asking, 'Will I not see him?' with a fainting heart, while his wife, looking at her unkempt hair, praises the deity in the shade of the cactus in the saline wasteland and worships with hands clasped over her hungry waist! Listen to the state of our prosperity. Whether you wish to receive gifts and eat, or set out to beg and bear your grief, both are within your reach, very near. When the battle clamor arose in the neighboring village, he appeared. Gathering the large herd of cattle, he and his brave warriors crossed the flood of discharged arrows using the drum as a raft. He brought victory, rescued the cattle from those who killed and seized them, and like the moon escaping the sharp teeth of the snake that encircles the world to make it lament, he rescued the cows and calves from the hands of the enemies. Having returned with the herd as a man of great fame, he shed his body like a snake shedding its skin, and departed to the world difficult to reach. His body, like a target post shaken by arrows on the steep bank of a small forest river, perished there. His name, which appeared with high fame, is now carved upon the hero-stone, adorned with the beautiful feathers of a gentle peacock, under a cloth canopy in a narrow path where others cannot crowd.","modern":"பாணனே! 'நான் அவனைக் காண மாட்டேனா?' என்று கேட்டுக்கொண்டு வரும் உனக்குச் சொல்கிறேன், கேள். அவனது மனைவி தன் கலைந்த கூந்தலைப் பார்த்து, கள்ளி மர நிழலில் உள்ள தெய்வத்தை வணங்கி, பசியால் வாடும் தன் வயிற்றைத் தொழுது அழுகிறாள். உனக்குக் கொடை வேண்டுமானாலும், அல்லது இரந்து வாழும் நிலை வேண்டுமானாலும், இரண்டுமே மிக அருகில் உள்ளன. பக்கத்து ஊரில் பூசல் எழுந்தபோது, அவன் தன் வீரர்களுடன் சென்று, பகைவர்களின் அம்பு மழையைக் கடந்து, கவரப்பட்ட பசுக்கூட்டங்களை மீட்டான். உலகை வருத்தும் பாம்பின் வாயிலிருந்து தப்பிய சந்திரன் போல, பகைவர் கைகளில் இருந்து கன்றுகளுடன் கூடிய பசுக்களை மீட்டுக் கொண்டு வந்து புகழ்பெற்றான். பாம்பு தன் சட்டையைக் கழற்றுவது போலத் தன் உடலை நீத்து, அவன் மேலுலகம் சென்றான். காட்டில் உள்ள சிற்றாற்றின் கரையில் அம்புகள் தைத்துச் சாய்ந்த இலக்குக் கம்பம் போல அவனது உடல் அங்கேயே அழிந்தது. அவனது சிறந்த புகழ் விளங்கும் பெயர், மயில் தோகையால் அலங்கரிக்கப்பட்டு, சிறிய வழியில் உள்ள பந்தலின் கீழ் நடப்பட்ட நடுகல்லில் மட்டுமே இப்போது உள்ளது.","explanation":"The poet Vaṭamōtaṅkiḻār addresses a bard (pāṇan) who has come seeking the generous hero, unaware of his death. The poem belongs to the Karantai tiṇai, which deals with the recovery of cattle stolen by enemies, and the tuṟai is Kaiyaṟunilai (helplessness/mourning). The poet describes the grief of the hero's wife, who worships the local deity in the harsh desert landscape, and contrasts this with the hero's past valor. The hero successfully rescued the cattle from the enemies, crossing a barrage of arrows, but eventually fell in battle. His body perished on a riverbank like a target post riddled with arrows, and now only his name remains, carved on a hero-stone (naṭukal) adorned with peacock feathers under a small canopy.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.45],[1.45,1.8],[1.8,2.47],[2.47,2.9],[2.9,3.2],[3.2,3.7],[3.7,4.7],[4.7,4.8],[4.8,5.2],[5.2,5.7],[5.7,6.8],[6.8,6.9],[6.9,7.2],[7.2,7.5],[7.5,8.7],[8.7,9.0],[9.0,9.2],[9.2,9.5],[9.5,9.5],[9.5,9.5],[9.5,9.5],[9.5,9.5],[9.5,13.1],[13.1,13.5],[13.5,13.7],[13.7,14.03],[14.2,14.6],[14.6,14.94],[15.29,15.8],[15.8,15.8],[15.8,16.6],[17.66,18.36],[18.36,18.67],[18.79,19.16],[19.16,19.86],[19.86,20.66],[20.66,21.16],[21.16,21.66],[21.66,22.16],[22.16,22.94],[22.94,23.36],[23.36,23.93],[23.93,24.26],[24.26,25.36],[25.36,25.76],[25.76,25.76],[25.76,26.46],[26.46,26.9],[26.9,27.13],[27.13,27.35],[27.35,28.46],[28.46,29.66],[29.66,29.86],[29.86,30.49],[30.49,30.96],[30.96,31.66],[31.66,31.96],[31.96,32.33],[32.41,32.86],[32.86,33.96],[33.96,34.36],[34.36,34.76],[34.76,34.96],[36.08,36.88],[36.88,37.18],[37.18,37.38],[37.38,37.88],[37.88,38.78],[38.8